  nodeAbstract: 
  nodeTextLayers:
  - Two insulin monomers join together by an intermolecular beta sheet to form a
    dimer.
  - An Insulin dimer is inactive for binding insulin receptors because its binding
    site is locked up in dimer interface.
  - Zinc is coordinated to 3 hisB10 (histine) residues in a dimer.
  - Two dimers with Zincs will attach first before attracting a third dimer to form
    a hexamer.
